  "claim_short": "Full counterexample to Conjecture 7.17 of arXiv:1811.05761. Let the positive i.i.d. weights be e and e^{-1} with equal probability and take x=sum k^{-3/5} e_k in ell^2. For each n, among ceil(e^n) disjoint length-n blocks the probability that none is all-e is at most exp(-(e/2)^n), which is summable. Borel-Cantelli therefore gives an all-e block for every sufficiently large n almost surely. Its single contribution...",
